    | Neural Social Grid | Tier 3 |  | Media | Bio | Consumer | 18 | 0 | 2 | 24 | 3 | 0 | 1 |
    | DAO Nation | Tier 3 |  | Crypto | Social | FinTech | 20 | 0 | 0 | 28 | 2 | 0 | 1 |
    | Asteroid Mining | Tier 3 |  | Robotics | Cloud | Deep Tech | 8 | 18 | 12 | 18 | 0 | 3 | 1 |
    | Planetary Wi-Fi | Tier 3 |  | Cloud | IoT | Infra | 6 | 16 | 8 | 16 | 0 | 3 | 1 |
  Cards can be onboarding.
  Cards can be red mode.
  Cards can be qa mode.
  Cards can be offline.
  Cards can have blue cubes, red cubes, new blue cubes and new red cubes.
  Cards can have cut blue cubes and cut red cubes.
  Cards can have bugs and fixed bugs.

Table:
  The talent deck is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  The agency row is a row in the center that everyone can see.
  The open job market is a row in the center that everyone can see.
  The seed deck is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  The growth deck is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  The seed market is a row in the center that everyone can see.
  The growth market is a row in the center that everyone can see.
  The open idea pool is a row in the center that everyone can see.
  The crash pile is a pile in the center that everyone can see.
  The box is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  Each player has a bench row that only they can see.
  Each player has a backlog row that only they can see.
  Each player has a research row that only they can see.
  Each player has a development row that everyone can see.
  Each player has an operations row that everyone can see.
  Each player has a development team row that everyone can see, where every card is on a card in their development.
  Each player has an ops team row that everyone can see, where some cards are on cards in their operations.
  Each player has a scouting row that only they can see.

Blue output:
  A software card's blue output is its output.
  A flex card's blue output is its output.
  A red mode card's blue output is 0.
  An onboarding card's blue output is 0.

Red output:
  A hardware card's red output is its output.
  A red mode card's red output is its output.
  A qa mode card's red output is 0.
  An onboarding card's red output is 0.

QA output:
  A qa card's qa output is its output.
  A qa mode card's qa output is 1.
  An onboarding card's qa output is 0.

Blue team output:
  A card's blue team output is the total blue output of the cards on it.
  A stalled card's blue team output is 0.

Red team output:
  A card's red team output is the total red output of the cards on it.
  A stalled card's red team output is 0.

QA team output:
  A card's qa team output is the total qa output of the cards on it.
  A stalled card's qa team output is 0.

Blue bandwidth:
  A card's blue bandwidth is its blue output.

Red bandwidth:
  A card's red bandwidth is its red output.

Blue need:
  A card's blue need is its blue cost.
  A card's blue need goes down by its cut blue cubes.

Red need:
  A card's red need is its red cost.
  A card's red need goes down by its cut red cubes.

Leading software:
  Only if it is a Senior Developer card.
  Only if one of:
    It is a software card.
    It is a flex card.
  Only if it is not onboarding.

Leading hardware:
  Only if it is a Senior Developer card.
  Only if one of:
    It is a hardware card.
    It is a flex card.
  Only if it is not onboarding.

Stalled:
  Only if it is in a development.
  Only if it is not a Tier 1 card.
  Only if one of:
    Its blue need is 0.
    No card on it is leading software.
  Only if one of:
    Its red need is 0.
    No card on it is leading hardware.

Fully led:
  Only if one of:
    It is a Tier 1 card.
    Its blue need is 0.
    Some card on it is leading software.
  Only if one of:
    It is a Tier 1 card.
    Its red need is 0.
    Some card on it is leading hardware.

Efficient in ops:
  Only if it is an Efficient card.
  Only if it is in an ops team.

Salary:
  An efficient in ops card's salary is 1.

Declarable:
  Only if one of:
    It is a flex card.
    It is a QA Skill card.

Rev:
  A card's rev goes up by the total rev bonus of the cards on it.
  A card's rev goes down by its bugs.
  A card's rev is at least 0.
  An offline card's rev is 0.

Rev bonus:
  A Viral Loop card's rev bonus is 3.

Portfolio points:
  A card's portfolio points is its val.
  An offline card's portfolio points is 0.

Bugged:
  Only if its bugs are more than 0.

Bug mark:
  A bugged card's bug mark is 1.

Attaching:
  Only if it is a Viral Loop card.

Spreading bugs:
  Only if it is a Viral Loop card.
  Only if it is not onboarding.

Viral:
  Only if some card on it is spreading bugs.

Feature complete:
  Only if its blue cubes are at least its blue need.
  Only if its red cubes are at least its red need.

Blue supply:
  A player's blue supply is the total blue bandwidth of the cards in their ops team.

Red supply:
  A player's red supply is the total red bandwidth of the cards in their ops team.

Blue demand:
  A player's blue demand is the total blue maint of the cards in their operations that are not offline.

Red demand:
  A player's red demand is the total red maint of the cards in their operations that are not offline.

Blue load:
  A player's blue load is the total blue maint of the cards in their operations.

Red load:
  A player's red load is the total red maint of the cards in their operations.

QA supply:
  A player's qa supply is the total qa output of the cards in their ops team.

Bug load:
  A player's bug load is the total bugs of the cards in their operations.

QA spent:
  A player's qa spent is the total fixed bugs of the cards in their operations.

Bugged products:
  A player's bugged products is the total bug mark of the cards in their operations.

Setup:
  Shuffle the talent deck.
  Shuffle the seed deck.
  Shuffle the growth deck.
  The market crash goes into the bottom fifth of the growth deck.
  The start player is chosen at random.
  A new Junior Software Dev goes to each bench.
  A new Junior Hardware Eng goes to each bench.
  A new Junior QA Tester goes to each bench.
  Deal 1 card from the seed deck to each backlog.

In every phase:
  When a player's turn starts:
    No card is onboarding.
  When the agency row has fewer than 4 cards:
    Only if the talent deck is not empty.
    Move the top card of the talent deck to the agency row.
  When the agency row has more than 4 cards:
    Move the top card of the agency row to the open job market.
  When the seed market has fewer than 2 cards:
    Only if the seed deck is not empty.
    Move the top card of the seed deck to the seed market.
  When the growth market has fewer than 2 cards:
    Only if the growth deck is not empty.
    Move the top card of the growth deck to the growth market.
  When the growth market has the market crash:
    Move the market crash from the growth market to the crash pile.
  When the open job market has more than 5 cards:
    Move the bottom card of the open job market to the box.
  When the open idea pool has more than 5 cards:
    Move the bottom card of the open idea pool to the box.
  When a card in a bench is red mode:
    It is not red mode.
  When a card in a bench is qa mode:
    It is not qa mode.
  When a card in the open job market is red mode:
    It is not red mode.
  When a card in the open job market is qa mode:
    It is not qa mode.
  When a Spaghetti Code card joins a card in a development:
    The card it joins gains 1 bug.

Phase: modes
  Hint: Choose what each flex Senior and the Fixer work on this turn: Blue or Red, or Bugs for the Fixer. Each keeps its mode until you change it.
  A player may declare a card in their development team.
    Only if it is declarable.
    Then:
      They choose one:
        Blue:
          Only if it is a flex card.
          It is not red mode.
        Red:
          It is red mode.
          It is not qa mode.
        QA:
          Only if it is a QA Skill card.
          It is qa mode.
          It is not red mode.
  A player may declare a card in their ops team.
    Only if it is declarable.
    Then:
      They choose one:
        Blue:
          Only if it is a flex card.
          It is not red mode.
        Red:
          It is red mode.
          It is not qa mode.
        QA:
          Only if it is a QA Skill card.
          It is qa mode.
          It is not red mode.
  A player may confirm their modes.
    Then:
      Go to ops check.
  When no card in their development team and their ops team is declarable, go to ops check.

Phase: ops check
  Hint: Your ops team can't run all your products. Switch some off until the rest fit your Blue and Red bandwidth, then confirm. A product switched off earns nothing.
  When this phase starts:
    Every card in their operations is not offline.
  A player may switch off a card in their operations.
    Only if it is not offline.
    Then:
      It is offline.
  A player may switch on a card in their operations.
    Only if it is offline.
    Then:
      It is not offline.
  A player may confirm the products online.
    Only if their blue supply is at least their blue demand.
    Only if their red supply is at least their red demand.
    Then:
      Go to income.
  When their blue supply is at least their blue load:
    Only if their red supply is at least their red load.
    Go to income.

Phase: income
  Hint: Pay every salary on your board. If you can't, or won't, let go of the staff you won't pay.
  When this phase starts:
    They get the total rev of the cards in their operations.
    For each card in their operations whose rev is more than 0, they get 1 market share.
  A player may let go of a card in their development team.
    Only if its salary is more than 0.
    Then:
      Move it to the open job market.
  A player may let go of a card in their ops team.
    Only if its salary is more than 0.
    Then:
      Move it to the open job market.
  A player may pay salaries.
    Only if they have at least the total salary of the cards in their development team and their ops team in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the total salary of the cards in their development team and their ops team.
      Go to actions.
  When the total salary of the cards in their development team and their ops team is 0, go to actions.

Phase: actions
  Players take turns.
  Hint: Spend 3 actions on hiring, drafting, research and your board. Greenlighting and dismissing cost no actions, though a product may need Licenses. Press a button, then pick the cards.
  A player may recruit a junior software dev.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least 2 capital.
    Then:
      They pay 2.
      A new Junior Software Dev goes to their bench.
  A player may recruit a junior hardware eng.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least 2 capital.
    Then:
      They pay 2.
      A new Junior Hardware Eng goes to their bench.
  A player may recruit a junior qa tester.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least 2 capital.
    Then:
      They pay 2.
      A new Junior QA Tester goes to their bench.
  A player may hire a card from the agency row to their bench.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least the card's cost in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the card's cost.
  A player may hire a card from the open job market to their bench.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least 1 capital.
    Then:
      They pay 1.
  A player may hire a card from the agency row to a card in their development.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least the card's cost in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the card's cost.
      It goes to their development team, on the target card.
  A player may hire a card from the agency row to their ops team.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if their operations is not empty.
    Only if it is not attaching.
    Only if they have at least the card's cost in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the card's cost.
  A player may hire a card from the agency row to a card in their operations.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if they have at least the card's cost in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the card's cost.
      If it is attaching, it goes to their ops team, on the target card.
      If it is not attaching, move it to their ops team.
  A player may greenlight a card in their backlog.
    Only if their development has fewer than 3 cards.
    Only if one of:
      The card has no requires.
      Some player has a card in their operations whose tag is the card's requires.
    Only if one of:
      The card has no also requires.
      Some player has a card in their operations whose tag is the card's also requires.
    Only if one of:
      The card has no requires.
      They have a card in their operations whose tag is the card's requires.
      They have at least the license in capital.
    Only if one of:
      The card has no also requires.
      They have a card in their operations whose tag is the card's also requires.
      They have at least the license in capital.
    Only if one of:
      The card has no requires.
      The card has no also requires.
      They have a card in their operations whose tag is the card's requires.
      They have a card in their operations whose tag is the card's also requires.
      They have at least 2 times the license in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the license to another player of their choice who has a card in their operations whose tag is the card's requires.
        Only if they have no card in their operations whose tag is the card's requires.
      They pay the license to another player of their choice who has a card in their operations whose tag is the card's also requires.
        Only if they have no card in their operations whose tag is the card's also requires.
      It loses its cut blue cubes.
      It loses its cut red cubes.
      They choose one:
        Only if they have a card in their operations that is not offline and whose sector is the card's sector.
        Only if the card is not an Infra card.
        Only if the card is not a Concept card.
        Cut 2 blue:
          Only if its blue cost is more than 1.
          Only if one of:
            Its blue cost is more than 2.
            Its red cost is more than 0.
          It gains 2 cut blue cubes.
        Cut 2 red:
          Only if its red cost is more than 1.
          Only if one of:
            Its red cost is more than 2.
            Its blue cost is more than 0.
          It gains 2 cut red cubes.
        Cut 1 of each:
          Only if its blue cost is more than 0.
          Only if its red cost is more than 0.
          Only if one of:
            Its blue cost is more than 1.
            Its red cost is more than 1.
          It gains 1 cut blue cube.
          It gains 1 cut red cube.
        Cut 1 blue:
          Only if its blue cost is 2.
          Only if its red cost is 0.
          It gains 1 cut blue cube.
        Cut 1 red:
          Only if its red cost is 2.
          Only if its blue cost is 0.
          It gains 1 cut red cube.
      Move it to their development.
  A player may assign some cards from their bench to a card in their development.
    It costs 1 action.
    Then:
      The picked cards go to their development team, on the target card.
  A player may assign some cards from their bench to their ops team.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if their operations is not empty.
    Only if no picked card is attaching.
  A player may assign some cards from their bench to a card in their operations.
    It costs 1 action.
    Then:
      The picked cards that are attaching go to their ops team, on the target card.
      The picked cards that are not attaching go to their ops team.
  A player may reassign a card from their development team to a card in their development.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if the card is not an Ego card.
    Only if it is not on the target card.
    Then:
      It goes to their development team, on the target card.
      It is onboarding.
  A player may reassign a card from their ops team to a card in their development.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if the card is not an Ego card.
    Then:
      It goes to their development team, on the target card.
      It is onboarding.
  A player may reassign a card from their ops team to a card in their operations.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if it is on a card.
    Only if it is not on the target card.
    Then:
      It goes to their ops team, on the target card.
      It is onboarding.
  A player may recall some cards from their ops team to their bench.
    It costs 1 action.
  A player may dismiss a card in their development team.
    Then:
      It is not onboarding.
      Move it to the open job market.
  A player may dismiss a card in their ops team.
    Then:
      It is not onboarding.
      Move it to the open job market.
  A player may draft a card from the seed market to their backlog.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if their backlog has fewer than 4 cards.
  A player may draft a card from the growth market to their backlog.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if their backlog has fewer than 4 cards.
  A player may draft a card from the open idea pool to their backlog.
    It costs 2 actions.
    Only if their backlog has fewer than 4 cards.
  A player may research the seed deck.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if their backlog has fewer than 4 cards.
    Only if the seed deck is not empty.
    Then:
      Deal up to 3 cards from the seed deck to their research.
      The research phase starts with them.
  A player may research the growth deck.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if their backlog has fewer than 4 cards.
    Only if the growth deck is not empty.
    Then:
      Deal up to 3 cards from the growth deck to their research.
      The research phase starts with them.
  A player may launch a card from their development to their operations.
    It costs 1 action.
    Only if it is feature complete.
    Only if it is fully led.
    Only if its bugs are 0.
    Then:
      Every card on it that is attaching goes to their ops team, staying on it.
      Every card on it that is not attaching goes to their ops team.
  A player may pivot a card in their development.
    It costs 1 action.
    Then:
      Every card on it whose trait is Ego goes to the open job market.
      Every card on it is onboarding.
      Every card on it goes to their bench.
      It loses its blue cubes.
      It loses its red cubes.
      It loses its cut blue cubes.
      It loses its cut red cubes.
      It loses its bugs.
      Move it to the open idea pool.
  A player may lay off some cards from their bench to the open job market.
    It costs 1 action.
    Then:
      Deal up to as many cards as they picked from the talent deck to their scouting.
      The sourcing phase starts with them.
  A player may end their actions.
    Then:
      Their actions go back to 0.
  When they have less than 1 action, go to engine.

Phase: research
  Hint: Keep one of the cards you drew. The rest go to the open idea pool.
  A player may keep a card in their research.
    Then:
      Move it to their backlog.
      Move their research to the open idea pool.
      Go back to the interrupted turn.
  When their research has the market crash:
    Move the market crash from their research to the crash pile.
    If the growth deck is not empty, move the top card of the growth deck to their research.
  When their research is empty:
    Go back to the interrupted turn.

Phase: sourcing
  Hint: Hire any of the cards you found at their printed cost, to your bench or straight onto your board. The rest go to the agency row.
  A player may hire some cards from their scouting to their bench.
    Only if they have at least the total cost of the picked cards in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the total cost of the picked cards.
  A player may hire some cards from their scouting to their ops team.
    Only if their operations is not empty.
    Only if no picked card is attaching.
    Only if they have at least the total cost of the picked cards in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the total cost of the picked cards.
  A player may hire some cards from their scouting to a card in their operations.
    Only if they have at least the total cost of the picked cards in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the total cost of the picked cards.
      The picked cards that are attaching go to their ops team, on the target card.
      The picked cards that are not attaching go to their ops team.
  A player may hire some cards from their scouting to a card in their development.
    Only if they have at least the total cost of the picked cards in capital.
    Then:
      They pay the total cost of the picked cards.
      The picked cards go to their development team, on the target card.
  A player may pass on the rest.
    Then:
      Move their scouting to the left end of the agency row.
  When their scouting is empty:
    Go back to the interrupted turn.

Phase: engine
  Hint: Your ops team's QA can't fix every Bug on your products. Clean one Bug at a time from the products you choose.
  When this phase starts:
    For each card in their development, its new blue cubes go up by its blue team output.
    For each card in their development, its new red cubes go up by its red team output.
    For each card in their development, its bugs go down by its qa team output.
  A player may clean a card in their operations.
    Only if its bugs are more than 0.
    Only if their qa supply is more than their qa spent.
    Then:
      It loses 1 bug.
      It gains 1 fixed bug.
  When their qa supply is at least their bug load:
    Only if their qa spent is 0.
    For each card in their operations, it loses its bugs.
    Go to commit.
  When their bugged products is 1:
    Only if their qa spent is 0.
    The cards in their operations lose bugs between them, up to their qa supply, first card first.
    Go to commit.
  When their qa spent is at least their qa supply:
    For each card in their operations, it loses its fixed bugs.
    Go to commit.

Phase: commit
  When this phase starts:
    For each card in their development, its blue cubes go up by its new blue cubes, up to its blue need.
    For each card in their development, its red cubes go up by its new red cubes, up to its red need.
    For each card in their development, it loses its new blue cubes.
    For each card in their development, it loses its new red cubes.
    Go to bench cleanup.

Phase: bench cleanup
  Hint: Your bench holds 5 cards. Discard the rest to the open job market.
  A player may discard a card in their bench.
    Only if their bench has more than 5 cards.
    Then:
      Move it to the open job market.
  When their bench has fewer than 6 cards, go to backlog cleanup.

Phase: backlog cleanup
  Hint: Your backlog holds 3 cards. Discard the rest to the open idea pool.
  A player may discard a card in their backlog.
    Only if their backlog has more than 3 cards.
    Then:
      Move it to the open idea pool.
  When their backlog has fewer than 4 cards:
    If they have no card in their ops team that is not onboarding and whose trait is Clean Code, each viral card in their operations gains 1 bug.
    The turn passes to the left.

Phase: final check
  Hint: After the last round your ops team can't run all your products. Switch products off, or back on, until those still on fit your Blue and Red bandwidth.
  When their blue supply is at least their blue load:
    Only if their red supply is at least their red load.
    Only if some card in their operations is offline.
    Every card in their operations is not offline.
  When their blue supply is at least their blue demand:
    Only if their red supply is at least their red demand.
    The final check passes to the left.
  A player may switch off a card in their operations.
    Only if it is not offline.
    Then:
      It is offline.
  A player may switch on a card in their operations.
    Only if it is offline.
    Then:
      It is not offline.

End:
  The game ends when the crash pile is not empty and the round is finished.
  Before the score, each player has the final check, in turn from the start player.
  Each player scores 1 point for every 5 capital.
  Each card in a player's operations scores its portfolio points.
  Each player scores 2 points for each market share.
  Each Tier 1 card in a player's backlog scores -2 points.
  Each Tier 2 card in a player's backlog scores -5 points.
  Each Tier 3 card in a player's backlog scores -10 points.
  The highest score wins, and tied players share the win.

